-- The scrutinee-borrowed conservatism PIN (perceus.ml ~1039-1057): the
-- scrutinee `xs` is free on only ONE path through the branch body (the
-- nested if's else side), not every path.  The current path-INSENSITIVE
-- approximation still treats the scrutinee as borrowed on this branch,
-- keeping br_vars alive on both sub-paths rather than a path-sensitive free
-- that risks a UAF for the genuine single-sub-path case; see
-- specs/perceus-invariants.md §6.  That conservatism is about the br_vars
-- `h` and `t`, and it is what this fixture pins.  The scrutinee ITSELF is no
-- longer leaked on the true side: since 2026-09-16 the cross-branch pass
-- includes the default arm in its "live elsewhere" union, so `xs` -- dead on
-- the true side, live on the else side, and owned by this arm because
-- add_scrutinee_free_for handed ownership into the body -- is released there
-- (specs/progress/2026-09-16-if-else-drops-the-dead-side.md).  `h` carries
-- its own inc_rc, so that release frees the Cons cell and not the value
-- returned.
--
-- The element type is String, not Int, on purpose: since 2026-09-28 borrow
-- inference decides field escapes per FIELD, so over List(Int) `xs` (whose
-- only escaping fields are the Int heads) is inferred BORROWED and the owned
-- scrutinee this fixture exists to pin never arises
-- (specs/progress/2026-09-28-field-escape-owns-per-field.md).
mod ScrutineeBorrowedConservatism do
  needs IO.Console
  fn first_or_recheck(xs : List(String), flag : Bool) : String do
    match xs do
      Cons(h, t) ->
        if flag do
          h
        else
          match xs do
            Cons(h2, _) -> h2
            Nil -> "none"
          end
        end
      Nil -> "empty"
    end
  end

  fn main(_cap_console : Cap(IO.Console)) do
    println(first_or_recheck(Cons("a", Nil), true))
  end
end
